three small bugs (possibly, unix HARD nh3.0h6):

1) priestly blessings (for being pious) are either very short lived
    or they don't survive save/restore.

2) objects in dark rooms become hidden when you walk away from them.
    i think that is appropriate, however when you're blind you can still
    see the location of those objects after feeling them. this is
    inconsistent with the sighted effects.

3) occasionally in the part of the dungeon where you might find a floor
    which seems like one you visited in a previous lifetime the doors
    are wrong. the doors should be "wrong" on the "deja-vu" floor.
    i've seen neighboring floors also have the wrong doors along
    with the right doors.

